  "question": {
    "text": "In an amplitude modulation, a modulating signal having amplitude of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> is superimposed with a carrier signal of amplitude <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Y</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> in first case. Then, in second case, the same modulating signal is superimposed with different carrier signal of amplitude <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>Y</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>. The ratio of modulation index in the two case respectively wil be :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Modulating index is stated as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mfrac></math>, where,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo></math>amplitude of modulating signal and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo></math>amplitude of carrier signal.</p><p>Now, for first case,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>X</mi><mi>Y</mi></mfrac></math></p><p>For second case,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>X</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>Y</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>Thus, the ratio of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mi>X</mi><mi>Y</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mi>X</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>Y</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>:</mo><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p>"
  }
}